----------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party runtime dependencies
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The build will pull the following libraries. Their licenses are
recorded in docs/adr/0015-no-telemetry-no-google-services.md and
checked at release time by a Gradle license-compatibility task.

  Bouncy Castle (org.bouncycastle:bcpg-jdk18on, bcprov-jdk18on)
    License: MIT
  ez-vcard (com.googlecode.ez-vcard:ez-vcard)
    License: New BSD
  OkHttp (com.squareup.okhttp3:okhttp)
    License: Apache 2.0
  Retrofit (com.squareup.retrofit2:retrofit)
    License: Apache 2.0
  kotlinx.serialization
    License: Apache 2.0
  kotlinx.coroutines
    License: Apache 2.0
  AndroidX (security-crypto, room, work-manager, biometric, credentials,
            activity, activity-compose, lifecycle-runtime-compose,
            appcompat, core-ktx)
    License: Apache 2.0
  Jetpack Compose (ui, material3, foundation, ui-tooling-preview,
                   compose-bom)
    License: Apache 2.0

Test-only (not packaged in the APK):

  JUnit 4, Kotest, Robolectric, OkHttp MockWebServer,
  AndroidX test-junit / test-runner / test-rules, Room testing
    Licenses: EPL 1.0 / Apache 2.0 / various permissive
  Android Lint API (com.android.tools.lint) — for the custom
    PcontactsSensitiveLog rule module in :tools:lint
    License: Apache 2.0

Dev-time only (not packaged, not imported at runtime):

  @protontech/crypto — used solely by the vector-capture script
    in tools/vectors/ to derive bcrypt-SHA-512 / SRP / OpenPGP
    reference vectors. The Kotlin port in :core:crypto verifies
    itself against the captured JSON; nothing from the npm
    package reaches the APK.
    License: GPL-3.0

